# Git Replay

Local-first Tauri app: React + TypeScript UI, Rust engine, system Git CLI.
Nothing is uploaded. There is no HTTP backend and no Postgres.

## Invariants (never violate)

1. **Git is authoritative.** System Git CLI only. Never reimplement git semantics. Never parse human-formatted git output — plumbing + `-z` only.
2. **Replay is the product.** Features answer questions about time, continuity, and progression. Code-review / PM features are out of scope.
3. **Raw history stays visible.** Never silently rewrite, hide, or replace commits. Chapters and filters are presentation.
4. **Offline by default.** Optional network (`gh`, BYO-key chat) must not break core replay.
5. **Cache is derived.** SQLite and memory caches are delete-safe. Deleting them recomputes; it never loses repo data.
6. **UI stays responsive.** Git/disk in Rust `spawn_blocking`. Highlighting and word-diffs in Web Workers. Previous/Next feels instant.

Read `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/decisions/` before touching boundaries. New ADRs: `docs/decisions/NNNN-kebab-title.md`.

## Where code lives (mandatory)

| Kind | Path |
|------|------|
| UI feature | `apps/desktop/src/features/<feature>/` |
| Shared widgets | `apps/desktop/src/components/` |
| Hooks | `apps/desktop/src/hooks/` |
| Pure TS + IPC + caches | `apps/desktop/src/lib/` |
| Zustand stores | `apps/desktop/src/stores/` |
| CSS | `apps/desktop/src/styles/` |
| Workers | `apps/desktop/src/workers/` |
| Git engine | `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/git/` |
| IPC types (Rust) | `.../git/types.rs` (mirror in `src/lib/types.ts`) |
| Thin IPC | `.../commands.rs` |
| Service layer | `.../state.rs` |
| Engine fixtures | `apps/desktop/src-tauri/tests/` |
| Architecture | `docs/` |

Do not put JSX in `lib/`, git parsing in `commands.rs`, or CSS in feature folders.

## Commands

From repo root: `make check` before considering work done. `make kill` on Windows before cargo rebuilds while the app is running.

Never commit `node_modules/`, `target/`, `fixtures/demo-repo/`, secrets, or `.env`.
